.SH NAME
upterm-config-path - Show the path to the config file


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBupterm config path [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the path of the config file, whether or not it exists.

.PP
Config file: /home/user/.config/upterm/config.yaml

.PP
The file is optional; 'upterm config edit' creates it.

.PP
Exit status: 0, or 1 on failure.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for path


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug logging (log file: /home/user/.local/state/upterm/upterm.log). A non-empty DEBUG turns it on too.


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  # Print the config file's path:
  upterm config path
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBupterm-config(1)\fP


